---
import multiModelImg from '/src/assets/media/take-b-1970s.jpg';
---
<section class="section" aria-labelledby="multimodel-heading">
  <div class="split reveal">
    <div class="split-text">
      <span class="sect-label">Multi-Model Generation</span>
      <h2 id="multimodel-heading">Every AI Model. One Shot. <span class="grad-text">You Pick the Winner.</span></h2>
      <p>Stop switching tabs between Runway, Kling, and Sora. Generate the same shot across every model from a single workspace &mdash; then pick the best take and move on.</p>
      <ul class="feat-list">
        <li><span class="check-icon">&#10003;</span> <span><strong>Side-by-side generation</strong> &mdash; render the same prompt across Kling, Veo, Sora, Runway, Grok, and more in one click.</span></li>
        <li><span class="check-icon">&#10003;</span> <span><strong>Take-based workflow</strong> &mdash; every generation is a &ldquo;take.&rdquo; Keep your favorites, discard the rest, regenerate anytime.</span></li>
        <li><span class="check-icon">&#10003;</span> <span><strong>Text-to-sequence</strong> &mdash; describe your scene once. 10zebra auto-splits it into structured shots and generates each one.</span></li>
        <li><span class="check-icon">&#10003;</span> <span><strong>Prompt history tracking</strong> &mdash; every take logs its exact prompt, model, settings, and references. Regenerate with one click.</span></li>
      </ul>
    </div>
    <div class="split-visual">
      <img src={multiModelImg.src}
        alt="10zebra multi-model workspace showing side-by-side 1970s motorsport video generation" loading="lazy" />
    </div>
  </div>
</section>